@@ -3,3 +3,18 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` returns the value that a JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) refers to inside a
+JSON document. The empty pointer `""` refers to the whole document; `"/foo/0"` refers to the first
+element of the array `foo`. Member names escape `/` as `~1` and `~` as `~0`.
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from './src/index.ts';
+
+resolvePointer({ foo: ['bar', 'baz'] }, '/foo/1'); // 'baz'
+```
+
+It throws an `Error` when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer, or when it does not resolve to a value
+of the document. A `null` value is returned as `null`.
