@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+---
+id: dl-001-resolvepointer-follows-rfc-6901-strictly-and-adds-no-dependency
+type: decision-log
+title: "resolvePointer follows RFC 6901 strictly and adds no dependency"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+The library is imported by other team projects, so its behaviour must follow the published standards
+it implements. JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) is the standard way to refer to a value inside a JSON document,
+and the README rules out runtime dependencies.
+
+## Decision
+
+- `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` is implemented in `src/index.ts`, with no runtime dependency.
+- Pointer syntax follows RFC 6901 exactly: the empty pointer is the whole document; each token is
+  unescaped with `~1` then `~0`; any other `~` is an error; array indexes are `0` or a non-zero digit
+  followed by digits, so leading zeros are rejected; the `-` index is not resolvable and is an error.
+- Object members are looked up as own properties only, so inherited names such as `constructor` do not
+  resolve.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Callers get the standard's behaviour, and other projects can rely on it.
+- Behaviour that the RFC leaves open or that a looser implementation might accept, such as leading
+  zeros in indexes, is rejected. A caller that needs leniency must normalise its pointers first.
