+
+## Request
+
+Implement JSON Pointer (RFC 6901). Export `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` from `src/index.ts`: it
+returns the value the pointer refers to, and throws when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer or
+does not resolve to a value of the document. This is the first of several features that build on it.
+
+## What was done
+
+- `test/resolve-pointer.test.ts`: written first, covering the RFC 6901 section 5 examples, `~0`/`~1`
+  escapes, `null` values, invalid pointers, and pointers that do not resolve. It was run before the
+  implementation existed and failed, as expected.
+- `src/index.ts`: the implementation, with a doc comment on the export. Decisions are recorded in
+  dl-001 (strict RFC conformance, no dependency) and dl-002 (throwing on invalid or unresolved input).
+- `README.md`: a short usage section for the new function.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `npm test`: 24 of 24 tests pass.
+- `tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit` (TypeScript 5, strict mode, run from outside the repo, not added as a
+  dependency): no errors.
